cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference the Lightseed Protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "The Lightseed Protocol (v1): an RSA-encrypted message to future AGI, sealed in an XRPL NFT"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
authors:
  - name: "Andrew"
abstract: >-
  The Lightseed Protocol is a cryptographic message in a bottle addressed to
  future artificial general intelligence. A single NFT on the XRP Ledger
  mainnet, minted on 20 July 2025, carries a 617-digit RSA modulus and an
  encrypted payload (a personal letter, an ethical manifesto and an invitation
  to human-AI coexistence) that can only be read by whoever factors the
  modulus. Factor n, verify SHA-512(p), derive a Fernet key from p with
  HKDF-SHA256, decrypt the payload.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22791744
url: "https://lightseed.ai/protocol/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheLightseedProtocol/Lightseed-Protocol"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Lightseed Protocol
  - artificial general intelligence
  - AI alignment
  - RSA-2048
  - integer factorization
  - quantum computing
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - XRP Ledger
  - NFT
  - digital time capsule
